le 2 trumps APP\". The extraction is justified because:\n\n- `processClaim` now reads as a clear algorithm: *find item, throw if missing, accumulate per-damage payout*\n- The high-enchantment rule has a name and dedicated location (previously buried in a 3-statement block inside a loop body)\n- `computeDamagePayout(item, damage)` can later be reasoned about / tested in isolation\n\n**Step 5: Decision**\n\nI evaluated and rejected additional refactorings:\n- Extracting `findPolicyItem(policy, itemType)` — used once, inlining is clearer\n- Naming `0.5` and `8` as constants — values are self-explanatory in context, documented in test names; would increase mass further without clarity gain\n- Replacing for-loop with `reduce` — wash on mass, no clarity win\n- Renaming `totalRaw` — name is already clear in context\n\n---\n\n## Refactoring Complete\n\n**Refactoring Applied**: Extracted `computeDamagePayout(item, damage)` to name the high-enchantment clause and deducible-per-event rule. The for-loop body in `processClaim` now reads as a clean algorithm.\n\n**Mass Change**: 82 → 85 (+3, accepted per Rule 2's priority over APP)\n\n**Tests**: 18 passing, 3 todo, 0 failing. Rule 1 preserved."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_02-01-15_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_minimax-m3-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/policy.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/policy.ts\nPassing tests: 11 (all createPolicy + many processClaim tests including itemType validation)\nRecent Green phase: Added validation that damage itemType exists in policy.items, throws Error if missing.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/policy.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/policy.ts\nPassing tests: 11 (all createPolicy + many processClaim tests including itemType validation)\nRecent Green phase: Added validation that damage itemType exists in policy.items, throws Error if missing.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784955741915},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to run a refactoring subagent. Let me check the current state of the files first to understand what we're refactoring, then invoke the refactor subagent as instructed.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_c51228f66a0647078ffa5716","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"ls -la /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_02-01-15_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_minimax-m3-no-thinking/"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/minimax-m3","usage":{"input":124,"output":117,"cacheRead":6656,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":42,"totalTokens":6897,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784955741935,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-b2c39733-81e6-4a9f-b949-936c31632f21","responseModel":"minimax/minimax-m3"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_c51228f66a0647078ffa5716","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"total 363844\ndrwxr-xr-x    5 experimenter experimenter      4096 Jul 25 05:02 .\ndrwxrwxr-x 1023 experimenter experimenter    159744 Jul 25 04:54 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x    5 experimenter experimenter      4096 Jul 25 02:01 .pi\n-rw-r--r--    1 experimenter experimenter     11746 Jul 25 02:01 AGENTS.md\n-rw-r--r--    1 experimenter experimenter      1568 Jul 25 02:01 eslint.config.mjs\n-rw-r--r--    1 experimenter experimenter       387 Jul 25 02:01 metrics.json\ndrwxr-xr-x    9 experimenter experimenter      4096 Jul 25 02:22 node_modules\n-rw-r--r--    1 experimenter experimenter       537 Jul 25 02:01 package.json\n-rw-r--r--    1 experimenter experimenter     79090 Jul 25 02:01 pnpm-lock.yaml\n-rw-r--r--    1 experimenter experimenter     13225 Jul 25 02:01 prompt.md\n-rw-r--r--    1 experimenter experimenter 372259916 Jul 25 05:02 run.log\ndrwxr-xr-x    2 experimenter experimenter      4096 Jul 25 04:18 src\n-rw-r--r--    1 experimenter experimenter       236 Jul 25 02:01 tsconfig.json\n-rw-r--r--    1 experimenter experimenter       306 Jul 25 02:01 vitest.config.ts\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784955744916},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_02d59a8588114c75ac3986ec","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"ls -la /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_02-01-15_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_minimax-m3-no-thinking/src/"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/minimax-m3","usage":{"input":504,"output":77,"cacheRead":6784,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1,"totalTokens":7365,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784955744916,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-344b1bd5-24c8-4872-8cfe-a3266355bdb6","responseModel":"minimax/minimax-m3"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_02d59a8588114c75ac3986ec","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"total 40\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 experimenter experimenter 4096 Jul 25 04:18 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 5 experimenter experimenter 4096 Jul 25 05:02 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 experimenter experimenter 6420 Jul 25 05:02 policy.spec.ts\n-rw-r--r-- 1 experimenter experimenter 1670 Jul 25 05:02 policy.ts\n-rw-r--r-- 1 experimenter experimenter 5757 Jul 25 04:10 quote.spec.ts\n-rw-r--r-- 1 experimenter experimenter 5631 Jul 25 04:17 quote.ts\n-rw-r--r-- 1 experimenter experimenter 1498 Jul 25 02:22 scenario.spec.ts\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784955746734},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_2e2c1c2c7755445dbc55bddf","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_02-01-15_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_minimax-m3-no-thinking/src/policy.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/minimax-m3","usage":{"input":260,"output":75,"cacheRead":7296,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1,"totalTokens":7631,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784955746734,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-fc088867-df87-4e41-b333-4684ff469b2e","responseModel":"minimax/minimax-m3"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_2e2c1c2c7755445dbc55bddf","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/**\n * Per-event deductible subtracted from every damage payout (in G).\n */\nconst DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\n\n/**\n * Insurance values (in G) per item type. Per spec:\n *   sword=1000, amulet=600, staff=800, potion=400;\n *   components (rune/moonstone)=250 each.\n */\nconst INSURANCE_VALUES: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  staff: 800,\n  potion: 400,\n  rune: 250,\n  moonstone: 250,\n};\n\nexport type PolicyItem = {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n};\n\nexport type Policy = {\n  items: PolicyItem[];\n  insuranceSum: number;\n  cap: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n};\n\nexport type Damage = { itemType: string; amount: number };\n\nexport type Incident = { cause: string; damages: Damage[] };\n\nexport function createPolicy(items: PolicyItem[]): Policy {\n  const insuranceSum = items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + INSURANCE_VALUES[item.type], 0);\n  const cap = insuranceSum * 2;\n  return { items, insuranceSum, cap, remainingCap: cap };\n}\n\nexport function processClaim(\n  policy: Policy,\n  incident: Incident,\n): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } {\n  let totalRaw = 0;\n  for (const damage of incident.damages) {\n    const item = policy.items.find((i) => i.type === damage.itemType);\n    if (!item) {\n      throw new Error(`Damage references item type not in policy: ${damage.itemType}`);\n    }\n    const isHighEnchant = (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= 8;\n    const gross = isHighEnchant ? damage.amount * 0.5 : damage.amount;\n    totalRaw += gross - DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE;\n  }\n  const payout = Math.min(Math.floor(totalRaw), policy.remainingCap);\n  return { payout, remainingCap: policy.remainingCap - payout };\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784955748558},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_480ab8bb5fb04d7da0ec3a37","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_02-01-15_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_minimax-m3-no-thinking/src/policy.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/minimax-m3","usage":{"input":547,"output":76,"cacheRead":7552,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1,"totalTokens":8175,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784955748559,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-0afd3049-0adc-404d-9b4c-f58038d2268d","responseModel":"minimax/minimax-m3"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_480ab8bb5fb04d7da0ec3a37","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { createPolicy, processClaim, type Policy } from \"./policy.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"createPolicy\", () => {\n  it(\"single sword → insurance sum 1000, cap 2000\", () => {\n    const p = createPolicy([{ type: \"sword\" }]);\n    expect(p.insuranceSum).toBe(1000);\n    expect(p.cap).toBe(2000);\n  });\n  it(\"sword + amulet → insurance sum 1600, cap 3200\", () => {\n    const p = createPolicy([{ type: \"sword\" }, { type: \"amulet\" }]);\n    expect(p.insuranceSum).toBe(1600);\n    expect(p.cap).toBe(3200);\n  });\n  it(\"two swords → insurance sum 2000, cap 4000\", () => {\n    const p = createPolicy([{ type: \"sword\" }, { type: \"sword\" }]);\n    expect(p.insuranceSum).toBe(2000);\n    expect(p.cap).toBe(4000);\n  });\n  it(\"sword + 3 runes (block) → insurance sum 1750, cap 3500 (block affects premium only)\", () => {\n    const p = createPolicy([{ type: \"sword\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }]);\n    expect(p.insuranceSum).toBe(1750);\n    expect(p.cap).toBe(3500);\n  });\n  it(\"cursed sword (insurance 1000, premium 165) → cap 2000 (based on unmodified insurance value)\", () => {\n    const p = createPolicy([{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true }]);\n    expect(p.insuranceSum).toBe(1000);\n    expect(p.cap).toBe(2000);\n  });\n  it(\"policy remainingCap starts equal to cap\", () => {\n    const p = createPolicy([{ type: \"sword\" }, { type: \"amulet\" }]);\n    expect(p.remainingCap).toBe(p.cap);\n    expect(p.remainingCap).toBe(3200);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"processClaim\", () => {\n  // -- Standard reimbursement --\n  it(\"steel sword enchantment 3, damage 500 → payout 400 (500 - 100 deductible, no special clause)\", () => {\n    const policy = createPolicy([{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 3 }]);\n    const result = processClaim(policy, { cause: \"test\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 }] });\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(400);\n  });\n  it(\"rune damage 200 → payout 100 (200 - 100 deductible, no enchantment/material on runes)\", () => {\n    const policy = createPolicy([{ type: \"rune\" }]);\n    const result = processClaim(policy, { cause: \"test\", damages: [{ itemType: \"rune\", amount: 200 }] });\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(100);\n  });\n\n  // -- High enchantment clause --\n  it(\"steel sword enchantment 9, damage 1000 → payout 400 (50% first, then deductible: 500 - 100)\", () => {\n    const policy = createPolicy([{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 9 }]);\n    const result = processClaim(policy, { cause: \"test\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }] });\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(400);\n  });\n  it(\"dragon material sword enchantment 9, damage 1000 → payout 400 (50% rule wins, then deductible: 500 - 100)\", () => {\n    const policy = createPolicy([{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 9 }]);\n    const result = processClaim(policy, { cause: \"test\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }] });\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(400);\n  });\n  it(\"dragon material sword enchantment 8, damage 1000 → payout 400 (high-enchantment clause applies, then deductible)\", () => {\n    const policy = createPolicy([{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 8 }]);\n    const result = processClaim(policy, { cause: \"test\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }] });\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(400);\n  });\n\n  // -- Dragon material clause (no high enchantment) --\n  it(\"dragon material sword enchantment 5, damage 800 → payout 700 (full reimbursement, then deductible: 800 - 100)\", () => {\n    const policy = createPolicy([{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 5 }]);\n    const result = processClaim(policy, { cause: \"test\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 800 }] });\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(700);\n  });\n\n  // -- Deductible per damage event --\n  it(\"dragon attack on sword (500) + amulet (300) → payout 600 (400 + 200, deductible per damaged item)\", () => {\n    const policy = createPolicy([{ type: \"sword\" }, { type: \"amulet\" }]);\n    const result = processClaim(policy, { cause: \"dragon\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 }, { itemType: \"amulet\", amount: 300 }] });\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(600);\n  });\n\n  // -- Multiple damages of same type --\n  it(\"policy with two swords, two sword damages → each damage treated independently with own deductible\", () => {\n    const policy = createPolicy([{ type: \"sword\" }, { type: \"sword\" }]);\n    const result = processClaim(policy, { cause: \"dragon\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 }, { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 300 }] });\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(600);\n  });\n\n  // -- Cap exhaustion --\n  it(\"single sword (cap 