ainingCap - payout };\n}\n```\n\n**Component count for `processClaim`:**\n- Constants (literals `0`, 2 error strings): 3 × 1 = 3\n- Bindings (policy, incident, totalRaw, damage, item, i, payout): 7 × 1 = 7\n- Invocations (incident.damages, find, i.type===, 2×Error, damage.amount<0, damage.amount, computeDamagePayout, Math.min, Math.floor, policy.remainingCap×2, -): ~14 × 2 = 28\n- Conditionals (if !item, if <0): 2 × 4 = 8\n- Loops (for-of): 1 × 5 = 5\n- Assignments (=0, +=): 2 × 6 = 12\n\n**Total mass for processClaim: ~63**\n\n## Step 4: Apply Refactoring\n\n**Refactoring**: Extract damage validation (item lookup + amount check) into a dedicated helper `validateDamage`. This separates concerns — `processClaim` becomes pure aggregation; the helper handles \"is this damage legitimate\".\n\n**Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**: The current loop body has THREE distinct responsibilities crammed in: (a) find the item, (b) validate amount, (c) compute payout. Extracting (a)+(b) into `validateDamage` makes each step self-documenting at the call site:\n\n```typescript\nfor (const damage of incident.damages) {\n  const item = validateDamage(policy, damage);\n  totalRaw += computeDamagePayout(item, damage);\n}\n```\n\nThe helper's name `validateDamage` reveals exactly what it does and its return type (`PolicyItem`) reveals that it doubles as the lookup."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_02b9c94c09a142a29acb0fe5","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"function findPolicyItem(policy: Policy, itemType: string): PolicyItem {\n  const item = policy.items.find((i) => i.type === itemType);\n  if (!item) {\n    throw new Error(`Damage references item type not in policy: ${itemType}`);\n  }\n  return item;\n}\n\nfunction validateDamage(policy: Policy, damage: Damage): PolicyItem {\n  if (damage.amount < 0) {\n    throw new Error(`Damage amount cannot be negative: ${damage.amount}`);\n  }\n  return findPolicyItem(policy, damage.itemType);\n}\n\nfunction computeDamagePayout(item: PolicyItem, damage: Damage): number {\n  const isHighEnchant = (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= 8;\n  const gross = isHighEnchant ? damage.amount * 0.5 : damage.amount;\n  return gross - DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE;\n}\n\nexport function processClaim(\n  policy: Policy,\n  incident: Incident,\n): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } {\n  let totalRaw = 0;\n  for (const damage of incident.damages) {\n    const item = validateDamage(policy, damage);\n    totalRaw += computeDamagePayout(item, damage);\n  }\n  const payout = Math.min(Math.floor(totalRaw), policy.remainingCap);\n  return { payout, remainingCap: policy.remainingCap - payout };\n}","oldText":"function computeDamagePayout(item: PolicyItem, damage: Damage): number {\n  const isHighEnchant = (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= 8;\n  const gross = isHighEnchant ? damage.amount * 0.5 : damage.amount;\n  return gross - DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE;\n}\n\nexport function processClaim(\n  policy: Policy,\n  incident: Incident,\n): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } {\n  let totalRaw = 0;\n  for (const damage of incident.damages) {\n    const item = policy.items.find((i) => i.type === damage.itemType);\n    if (!item) {\n      throw new Error(`Damage references item type not in policy: ${damage.itemType}`);\n    }\n    if (damage.amount < 0) {\n      throw new Error(`Damage amount cannot be negative: ${damage.amount}`);\n    }\n    totalRaw += computeDamagePayout(item, damage);\n  }\n  const payout = Math.min(Math.floor(totalRaw), policy.remainingCap);\n  return { payout, remainingCap: policy.remainingCap - payout };\n}"}],"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_02-01-15_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_minimax-m3-no-thinking/src/policy.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/minimax-m3","usage":{"input":255,"output":1624,"cacheRead":12032,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":486,"totalTokens":13911,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"tool