me":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Step 5: Calculate New APP Mass\n\nThe change adds one binding (`policy`). Everything else unchanged.\n\n- Constants: 5\n- Bindings: 7 (was 6, +1 for `policy`)\n- Invocations: 6 (mass 12)\n- Conditionals: 2 (mass 8)\n- Loops: 1 (mass 5)\n- Assignments: 1 (mass 6)\n\n**Mass: 43 (was 42, +1)**\n\nRule 2 (clarity) trumps APP — the +1 binding is justified because it names the entity being mutated and eliminates the repeated `policies[step.policyIndex]` indexing.\n\n## Step 6: Document Decision\n\n**Refactoring Applied:**\n- **Naming**: Kept all existing names — they clearly reveal intent (`runScenario`, `QuoteStep`, `ClaimStep`, `Step`, `Scenario`, `StepResult`, `QuoteResult`, `ClaimResult`).\n- **Clarity (Rule 2)**: Extracted `const policy = policies[step.policyIndex]` in the else branch. The entity being mutated now has a name, and `processClaim` / `policy.remainingCap = ...` reads as \"process the claim on this policy, then update its cap\" instead of three references to `policies[step.policyIndex]`.\n- **Duplication (Rule 3)**: None found.\n- **Fewest Elements (Rule 4)**: Considered extracting `runQuoteStep` / `runClaimStep` helpers but rejected — the function is already focused (one responsibility: iterate steps), each branch is short, and extraction would add elements without a clarity gain.\n\n**Benefits:**\n- The else branch now reads as a clear sequence: look up the policy → process the claim → persist the updated cap → record the result.\n- The comment about persisting the cap still applies; `policy.remainingCap = result.remainingCap` is now self-evidently a mutation of that named entity.\n\n## Step 7: Report Completion\n\n```\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Extracted `policy` local in the else branch of `runScenario` (Rule 2 clarity win)\n**Mass Change**: 42 -> 43 (+1 binding, justified by Rule 2)\n**Tests**: All 55 passing (4 todo remain in scenario spec for CLI subprocess features)\n**Lint**: Clean\n```\n\n**Refactored function:**\n```typescript\nexport function runScenario(scenario: Scenario): { results: StepResult[] } {\n  const results: StepResult[] = [];\n  const policies: Policy[] = [];\n  for (const step of scenario.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const isFollowup = policies.length > 0;\n      const premium = quotePremium(step.items, scenario.customer, { isFollowup });\n      policies.push(createPolicy(step.items));\n      results.push({ premium });\n    } else {\n      // processClaim returns the new cap as a value; persist it on the policy\n      // so subsequent claims against the same policy see the updated cap.\n      const policy = policies[step.policyIndex];\n      const result = processClaim(policy, step.incident);\n      policy.remainingCap = result.remainingCap;\n      results.push(result);\n    }\n  }\n  return { results };\n}\n```"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_02-01-15_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_minimax-m3-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/scenario.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/scenario.ts\nPassing tests: 11 scenario tests now passing\nRecent Green phase: All error scenarios verified to throw correctly via existing validation in quote.ts and policy.ts.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/scenario.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/scenario.ts\nPassing tests: 11 scenario tests now passing\nRecent Green phase: All error scenarios verified to throw correctly via existing validation in quote.ts and policy.ts.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784957523334},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinkin