ontent"},{"type":"text","text":"## Step 5: Calculate New APP Mass\n\nThe change adds one binding (`policy`). Everything else unchanged.\n\n- Constants: 5\n- Bindings: 7 (was 6, +1 for `policy`)\n- Invocations: 6 (mass 12)\n- Conditionals: 2 (mass 8)\n- Loops: 1 (mass 5)\n- Assignments: 1 (mass 6)\n\n**Mass: 43 (was 42, +1)**\n\nRule 2 (clarity) trumps APP — the +1 binding is justified because it names the entity being mutated and eliminates the repeated `policies[step.policyIndex]` indexing.\n\n## Step 6: Document Decision\n\n**Refactoring Applied:**\n- **Naming**: Kept all existing names — they clearly reveal intent (`runScenario`, `QuoteStep`, `ClaimStep`, `Step`, `Scenario`, `StepResult`, `QuoteResult`, `ClaimResult`).\n- **Clarity (Rule 2)**: Extracted `const policy = policies[step.policyIndex]` in the else branch. The entity being mutated now has a name, and `processClaim` / `policy.remainingCap = ...` reads as \"process the claim on this policy, then update its cap\" instead of three references to `policies[step.policyIndex]`.\n- **Duplication (Rule 3)**: None found.\n- **Fewest Elements (Rule 4)**: Considered extracting `runQuoteStep` / `runClaimStep` helpers but rejected — the function is already focused (one responsibility: iterate steps), each branch is short, and extraction would add elements without a clarity gain.\n\n**Benefits:**\n- The else branch now reads as a clear sequence: look up the policy → process the claim → persist the updated cap → record the result.\n- The comment about persisting the cap still applies; `policy.remainingCap = result.remainingCap` is now self-evidently a mutation of that named entity.\n\n## Step 7: Report Completion\n\n```\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Extracted `policy` local in the else branch of `runScenario` (Rule 2 clarity win)\n**Mass Change**: 42 -> 43 (+1 binding, justified by Rule 2)\n**Tests**: All 55 passing (4 todo remain in scenario spec for CLI subprocess features)\n**Lint**: Clean\n```\n\n**Refactored function:**\n```typescript\nexport function runScenario(scenario: Scenario): { results: StepResult[] } {\n  const results: StepResult[] = [];\n  const policies: Policy[] = [];\n  for (const step of scenario.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const isFollowup = policies.length > 0;\n      const premium = quotePremium(step.items, scenario.customer, { isFollowup });\n      policies.push(createPolicy(step.items));\n      results.push({ premium });\n    } else {\n      // processClaim returns the new cap as a value; persist it on the policy\n      // so subsequent claims against the same policy see the updated cap.\n      const policy = policies[step.policyIndex];\n      const result = processClaim(policy, step.incident);\n      policy.remainingCap = result.remainingCap;\n      results.push(result);\n    }\n  }\n  return { results };\n}\n```"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/minimax-m3","usage":{"input":24,"output":990,"cacheRead":30464,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":303,"totalTokens":31478,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784957781672,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-68b4ea5d-d69c-4c39-9966-fe9e1fc7c551","responseModel":"minimax/minimax-m3"}],"stderr":"","usage":{"input":9822,"output":15736,"cacheRead":276480,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"contextTokens":31478,"turns":16},"model":"requesty/tensorx/minimax-m3","stopReason":"stop"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784957799514},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I need to work on the CLI subprocess tests. I need to create cli.ts.\n\nLet me first check the scenario.ts to see what changes the refactor made.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_c08ef0eceb4b46f9bf9f02db","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_02-01-15_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_minimax-m3-no-thinking/src/scenario.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/minimax-m3","usage":{"input":720,"output":110,"cacheRead":74112,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":36,"totalTokens":74942,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784957799521,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-a67b7b55-160f-4499-b872-36a4bb98ff2e","responseModel":"minimax/minimax-m3"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_c08ef0eceb4b46f9bf9f02db","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { createPolicy, processClaim, type Policy, type Incident } from \"./policy.js\";\nimport { quotePremium, type QuoteItem, type Customer } from \"./quote.js\";\n\nexport type QuoteStep = {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: QuoteItem[];\n};\n\nexport type ClaimStep = {\n  op: \"claim\";\n  /**\n   * Index into the scenario's policies array (0-based, in quote-order).\n   * The policies array is grown by each quote step earlier in the scenario.\n   */\n  policyIndex: number;\n  incident: Incident;\n};\n\nexport type Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\nexport type Scenario = {\n  customer: Customer;\n  steps: Step[];\n};\n\nexport type QuoteResult = { premium: number };\nexport type ClaimResult = { payout: number; remainingCap: number };\nexport type StepResult = QuoteResult | ClaimResult;\n\nexport function runScenario(scenario: Scenario): { results: StepResult[] } {\n  const results: StepResult[] = [];\n  const policies: Policy[] = [];\n  for (const step of scenario.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const isFollowup = policies.length > 0;\n      const premium = quotePremium(step.items, scenario.customer, { isFollowup });\n      policies.push(createPolicy(step.items));\n      results.push({ premium });\n    } else {\n      // processClaim returns the new cap as a value; persist it on the policy\n      // so subsequent claims against the same policy see the updated cap.\n      const policy = policies[step.policyIndex];\n      const result = processClaim(policy, step.incident);\n      policy.remainingCap = result.remainingCap;\n      results.push(result);\n    }\n  }\n  return { results };\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784957803445},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. Now I need to handle the CLI tests. The tests use subprocess to test the CLI.\n\nLet me activate test 38.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"## Red -- Test 38: CLI reads JSON from stdin, writes JSON to stdout for valid scenario"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_7be93f37d8be4da893c3fed2","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"  it(\"reads JSON from stdin, writes JSON to stdout for valid scenario\", async () => {\n    const input = JSON.stringify({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    const result = await runCli(input);\n    expect(result.exitCode).toBe(0);\n    expect(JSON.parse(result.stdout)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n    expect(result.stderr).toBe(\"\");\n  });","oldText":"  it.todo(\"reads JSON from stdin, writes JSON to stdout for valid scenario\");"}],"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_02-01-15_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_minimax-m3-no-thinking/src/scenario.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/minimax-m3","usage":{"input":437,"output":293,"cacheRead":74880,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":29,"totalTokens":75610,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784957803448,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-1054a2f6-d0b3-4688-ac2f-7eb7624959ed","responseModel":"minimax/minimax-m3"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_7be93f37d8be4da893c3fed2","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_02-01-15_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation